{"summary":"Accept the two amendments that fix a real internal accounting invariant and remove unnecessary disabled-path allocations; reject the two whose factual premises are already false in the current tree.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-6a5fe401","decision":"accept","rationale":"`alk_budget` is maintained as a running shared resource limit alongside `do_budget`. After AOB it is decremented, after comammox it is not. Nothing currently reads it later, so this is latent rather than user-visible, but it still leaves the internal budget state inconsistent with the alkalinity actually charged that tick. Applying the same decrement after comammox is low risk and preserves the bookkeeping invariant for any later consumer of remaining alkalinity budget."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-9ac12929","decision":"accept","rationale":"`StageTrace::metric()` always constructs and stores a `BudgetMetric` with an owned `String`, but those metrics are only consumed when a budget ledger is active. When `ctx.budget` is `None`, the work is pure overhead and is dropped immediately. Guarding metric collection on budget activity is behavior-preserving, removes needless heap churn on the disabled path, and keeps the tracing/budget split cleaner."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-c283b14f","decision":"reject","rationale":"The stated defect is not present in the current repository state. `crates/tank_core/tests/nitrification_alkalinity.rs` is already tracked, so this is not an actual gap in the reviewed change set."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-beff8673","decision":"reject","rationale":"The premise is outdated. `NitrogenCycleOutput` already exposes both `alkalinity_consumed_meq` and `alkalinity_produced_meq`, and the engine already emits both corresponding metrics and trace notes. Future denitrification work may still extend attribution further, but the specific claimed consumed-versus-returned API/trace gap does not exist in the current code."}]}